1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,837
You don't have to build every
workflow from a blank page.

2
00:00:03,837 --> 00:00:08,579
In this lesson, you'll use a ready-made
recipe to set up missed call text back in

3
00:00:08,579 --> 00:00:13,205
about two minutes, and learn how to reuse
your own best workflows as templates.

4
00:00:14,055 --> 00:00:15,429
Click Create Workflow.

5
00:00:15,429 --> 00:00:20,364
Below Start from Scratch, you'll find
the recipes: ready-made workflows for the

6
00:00:20,364 --> 00:00:22,426
jobs almost every business needs.

7
00:00:23,277 --> 00:00:26,845
There's appointment confirmation
and reminders, Fast Five,

8
00:00:26,845 --> 00:00:31,704
which contacts new leads within five
minutes, review requests, no-show nurture,

9
00:00:31,704 --> 00:00:36,010
missed call text back, a birthday
template, and customer reactivation.

10
00:00:36,010 --> 00:00:39,701
Each one is a full workflow you
can change however you like.

11
00:00:39,701 --> 00:00:42,223
Think of them as a tested starting point,

12
00:00:42,223 --> 00:00:46,406
built around the situations that
cost businesses the most customers.

13
00:00:47,255 --> 00:00:49,038
Let's use Missed Call Text Back.

14
00:00:49,038 --> 00:00:52,158
When you miss a call, it texts
the caller straight away,

15
00:00:52,158 --> 00:00:55,167
so they don't just ring the
next business on the list.

16
00:00:55,167 --> 00:00:58,844
Click it to preview the trigger
and the actions before you commit.

17
00:00:59,694 --> 00:01:01,123
Click Use this recipe.

18
00:01:01,123 --> 00:01:06,383
Kyntlo creates a new workflow with everything
already in place, saved as a draft.

19
00:01:06,383 --> 00:01:10,538
Nothing runs until you publish
it, so you can explore it safely,

20
00:01:10,538 --> 00:01:12,811
and change anything you like first.

21
00:01:13,660 --> 00:01:15,498
Always check the trigger first.

22
00:01:15,498 --> 00:01:20,182
It's Call Status, filtered to calls with
no answer, coming in to your business.

23
00:01:20,182 --> 00:01:24,214
That way it only texts people who
called you and didn't get through.

24
00:01:25,127 --> 00:01:27,585
Then make the message sound like you.

25
00:01:27,585 --> 00:01:31,638
Open the SMS, replace the text
with your own words, and save.

26
00:01:31,638 --> 00:01:36,288
Mention your business name, so the
caller knows exactly who's texting.

27
00:01:36,288 --> 00:01:41,337
A short, warm message that invites a
reply works far better than a long one.

28
00:01:42,152 --> 00:01:45,234
Give it a clear name, switch
it to Publish, and save.

29
00:01:45,234 --> 00:01:49,652
That's a complete missed call text back
system, set up in about two minutes.

30
00:01:50,501 --> 00:01:52,168
Recipes are one shortcut.

31
00:01:52,168 --> 00:01:54,236
Your own workflows are another.

32
00:01:54,236 --> 00:01:58,970
Back in the list, open the menu next
to any workflow, and choose Clone.

33
00:01:58,970 --> 00:02:04,572
You get an exact copy as a draft, ready to
adapt, for a new offer or a new location.

34
00:02:05,423 --> 00:02:09,238
As your list grows, use Create
Folder to keep things tidy.

35
00:02:09,238 --> 00:02:13,514
Group workflows by purpose, like
leads, appointments and reviews,

36
00:02:13,514 --> 00:02:16,868
so you and your team can
always find the right one.

37
00:02:16,868 --> 00:02:22,065
A tidy list also makes it much easier to
spot old workflows you no longer need.

38
00:02:22,964 --> 00:02:24,009
Here's a pro tip.

39
00:02:24,009 --> 00:02:27,266
A recipe is a starting point,
not a finished product.

40
00:02:27,266 --> 00:02:31,199
Before you publish one, check
three things: the trigger filters,

41
00:02:31,199 --> 00:02:34,333
the wording of every message,
and the settings tab.

42
00:02:34,333 --> 00:02:36,422
Then run a quick test on yourself.

43
00:02:37,271 --> 00:02:40,184
You can now set up proven
workflows in minutes.

44
00:02:40,184 --> 00:02:44,027
Next, we'll connect Kyntlo to
your other tools, with webhooks,

45
00:02:44,027 --> 00:02:46,134
Google Sheets and premium actions.

46
00:02:46,134 --> 00:02:47,001
See you there!
